      RESIDUE| # Zene Studio 0.1.0-alpha: known limitations
      RESIDUE| What this alpha does **not** do, in the order you are likely to hit it. If something here surprises
      RESIDUE| you, that is this page's fault: report it and it gets added.
      RESIDUE| - **This is an alpha.** Some areas are unfinished and crashes are possible.
      RESIDUE| - **Keep backups.** Files saved by this build may not open in a later build, in an older build, or
      RESIDUE|   in LMMS. Copy the project folder or use File > Save As before you open anything here, and keep
      RESIDUE|   the original. See [Your projects](#your-projects).
      RESIDUE| - **The builds are unsigned.** Windows SmartScreen and macOS Gatekeeper warn about an unknown
      RESIDUE|   developer. The one-time steps are in [Getting it running](#getting-it-running). Do not answer
      RESIDUE|   either warning by turning protection off. The release page shows a SHA-256 digest next to each
      RESIDUE|   file; check your download before you run it.
      RESIDUE| - **Packages come from the release page, and only from there.** Build jobs upload packages for a
      RESIDUE|   tag build or a manual CI run, never for an ordinary push, and only the platforms whose build job
      RESIDUE|   is green have packages. Check the release page for the current set.
      RESIDUE| ## Getting it running
      RESIDUE| ### Linux
      RESIDUE| - **The AppImage needs FUSE 2.** On a distribution without it the file does not start, and
      RESIDUE|   double-clicking it may do nothing. Install the FUSE 2 library and try again:
      RESIDUE|   `sudo apt install libfuse2` (on Ubuntu 24.04 the package is named `libfuse2t64`).
      RESIDUE| - **Still not starting? Run it unpacked:** `--appimage-extract-and-run`. Treat this as a fallback:
      RESIDUE|   it unpacks the app on every start, so it is slower.
      RESIDUE| - **There is no menu entry.** AppImages do not add themselves to the applications menu, so the app
      RESIDUE|   appears there only if you install a desktop-integration helper. Start it from the file or from a
      RESIDUE|   terminal.
      RESIDUE| ### Windows
      RESIDUE| - **SmartScreen blocks the first run of the unsigned installer.** Click *More info*, then *Run
      RESIDUE|   anyway*; the installer runs normally after that. Do not turn SmartScreen off.
      RESIDUE| ### macOS
      RESIDUE| - **Gatekeeper refuses the first launch.** The app is ad-hoc signed only (no Developer ID, no
      RESIDUE|   notarisation), so macOS cannot verify the developer. Click **Done** on the warning, then open
      RESIDUE|   **System Settings > Privacy & Security**, scroll to **Security**, click **Open Anyway**, and
      RESIDUE|   confirm. On macOS 15 (Sequoia) and later the old "right-click, then Open" shortcut does not
      RESIDUE|   work. Do not turn Gatekeeper off.
      RESIDUE| ## Scripting and AI DSP
      RESIDUE| - **WASM scripting is compiled out of these builds.** The sandbox needs the wasmtime C API at
      RESIDUE|   configure time; without it the effect is skipped entirely, and the binary reports
      RESIDUE|   `WANT_WASM=OFF`. Lua 5.4 scripting is in.
      RESIDUE| - **Offline stem separation is compiled out of these builds.** It is opt-in at configure time
      RESIDUE|   (`-DWANT_STEM_SPLIT=ON`) and no CI job sets it, so the binary reports `WANT_STEM_SPLIT=OFF`.
      RESIDUE| - **No project-format stability promise yet.** A project saved by this alpha may not open in an
      RESIDUE|   older build, in LMMS, or in a previous alpha. Do not try to open a v0.1 project in an older
      RESIDUE|   macOS carries an ad-hoc signature only, so Gatekeeper refuses the first launch until you use
      RESIDUE|   **System Settings > Privacy & Security > Open Anyway**. The per-platform steps are in
      RESIDUE|   [Getting it running](#getting-it-running).
      RESIDUE| - If the release is not published yet, the only builds in existence are CI packages from earlier
      RESIDUE|   runs; those report `LMMS 1.3.0-alpha`, while a build from the release tag reports
      RESIDUE|   `LMMS 0.1.0-alpha`. The string is build provenance, not a second product name.
